WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.640
Hey, David, do you think that Donald Trump's
new tone around Corona virus, taking it more

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.809
seriously and wearing or carrying around the
mask is going to help him turn the election

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:09.809
around?

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.889
I don't think so, no.

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:12.410
I mean, I think it's too little, too.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:16.500
You know, for the first four or five months
of coronavirus in the United States, Trump

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.010
continued to say everything's fine.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.161
Refuse to wear masks.

00:00:20.161 --> 00:00:22.980
Masks are, you know, it's your choice.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.350
You can wear it or not wear it or whatever.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.460
We have 15 cases.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.120
It'll soon go to zero, et cetera, et cetera,
et cetera.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.840
In the last 10 to 14 days, we saw Trump with
a mask out in public.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.360
He keeps it in his suit pocket during his
corona virus press briefings to be able to

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.980
pull it out like a prop at anytime.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.770
He has actually said some things that are
more sober, like it could get worse before

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:44.770
it gets better.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.540
And on and on and on.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.760
Will this turn around the election for Donald
Trump?

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.520
I don't believe so.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.800
I don't believe so, because, number one, the
cat is sort of out of the bag from the standpoint

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.540
of corona virus, even if indeed the Trump
administration is now covering up cases since

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.350
the changeover from reporting data to the
CDC, instead reporting data to Health and

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:07.350
Human Services.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.670
We covered that earlier this week.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.159
People know that they're unemployed.

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:12.659
People know that their friends are unemployed.

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:14.460
People know the economy is a catastrophe.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.009
People disapprove of Trump's handling of racial
issues, which is the third most important

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:20.369
issue going into November.

00:01:20.369 --> 00:01:26.229
So I think Trump putting a mask on now and
saying this is tough is simply not going to

00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:27.229
be enough.

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:32.020
Now, could it still be important as far as
keeping people safe?

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.179
In other words, will Trump's supporters start
wearing masks because Trump has worn a mask?

00:01:37.179 --> 00:01:41.859
I seriously hope so, because that is one of
the most important things that we can do.

00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:44.219
We covered on a bonus show earlier this week.

00:01:44.219 --> 00:01:48.880
There's a lot of hygiene theater, you know,
restaurants announcing we're going to close

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:56.810
an hour early to spray with some disinfectant,
the entire restaurant or whatever.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:00.460
There's really no evidence that significant
contagion is happening through surfaces in

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:06.859
that way, you know, cleaning tables and seating
surfaces between guests should be more than

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:07.859
enough.

00:02:07.859 --> 00:02:12.829
So there's like hygiene theater stuff that
does not really seem to hold down contagion.

00:02:12.829 --> 00:02:17.860
Wearing a mask does wearing a mask when you're
indoors, avoiding crowds.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.500
That's the stuff that really matters.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:25.340
And so if Trump carrying his mask around helps
more Trump supporters feel OK putting on a

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.319
mask, then that's great.

00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:30.750
And I would be crazy to oppose that and I
don't oppose it.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.189
Now, there's one other component to this.

00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:40.989
It is possible that Trump wearing a mask and
then more people wearing masks as a result

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:44.530
will increase the number of people that feel
comfortable going and voting in person in

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.530
November.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:49.880
Maybe there were people in November who maybe
were going to stay home, but now we're going

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.020
to go out now.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.630
I'm thinking of Democrats.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.140
What I mean is the following.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.319
If you're a Trump supporter and you're already
not paying attention to masks, you're going

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:00.060
to go out and vote in person in November.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:05.390
If you're a Democrat and you care about masks
and they aren't mandatory or a lot of people

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:11.280
aren't wearing them, you might stay home because
others don't plan to wear a mask.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:17.110
You seeing more Republicans wearing masks
might make you, as a Democrat, more comfortable

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.069
going out to vote in November.

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:20.069
And that would be great.

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:25.130
It would be great if Trump wearing a mask
increases everybody's mask compliance, which

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:30.370
makes more Democrats feel comfortable going
out and safely voting in November.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.680
If the death toll goes down significantly.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.900
That may actually be what helps Trump the
most.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.239
And the mask wearing could be part of it.

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:41.700
But it's a long path, right?

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.939
The mask wearing you need eight to 10 weeks
to flatten the case curve.

00:03:44.939 --> 00:03:49.280
It's about another 15, 20 days to deal with
the deaths.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.430
And then we're at Election Day.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.560
So I just don't know that the timing is going
to work out.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:58.050
Unemployment going down, stock market continuing
to climb, I don't think is going to do very

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.709
much for Donald Trump in terms of the polls.

00:04:00.709 --> 00:04:05.670
It really fundamentally comes down to can
Donald Trump avoid another major mistake,

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:09.219
like the response to the George Floyd protest
was a disaster.

00:04:09.219 --> 00:04:12.829
Trump's now more than 20 points underwater
on racial relations compared to Joe Biden

00:04:12.829 --> 00:04:14.200
disaster.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.980
Trump's early coronavirus response to disaster,
you know, carrying the mask around now I think

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.670
is too little, too late.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:24.300
The resulting economic damage and the fact
that twelve hundred bucks is what's gone out

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.720
to some people.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:26.720
Disaster.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.810
If Trump can avoid another major mistake,
if deaths do start to go down.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:35.570
If the economy does start to improve in a
real, measurable way, that will help Donald

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:36.570
Trump.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:37.570
But ultimately, he's desperate.

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.570
He knows it.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:43.770
And it is now about lying about the numbers
to try to hide them and and trying to suppress

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:44.770
the vote.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:47.920
Which is why we have to work really, really
hard to prevent that from happening.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:52.450
We have to overwhelm the vote by so much that
the voter suppression Trump will plan to do

00:04:52.450 --> 00:06:52.570
this planning to do won't be enough to hand
him a reelection victory.

